accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report  ms 08  removed_accession_id  case  ms 08  removed_accession_id  removed_patient_name  date taken  removed_date source care unit  rad mammography meei mrn  removed_date path subspecialty service  breast 1 results to  michelle c specht  m d  phoebe e freer  m d  elizabeth a rafferty  m d  resident  colleen a lamb  m d  signed out by  ronald balassanian  m d  clinical data  the patient is a 35 year old woman with recent left subareolar excision of papilloma  udh and left breast excision and re excision with positive margins for dcis and phyllodes tumor  a breast mri after the second surgery demonstrated a solid enhancing mass at 11 00 o clock far from surgical site  which appears solid on ultrasound  the lesion may represent a fibroadenoma but there is a small satellite or contiguous focus so the differential diagnosis includes fba versus phyllodes versus papilloma versus other  please rush for surgical management  final diagnosis  breast  left   core biopsy  low grade fibro epithelial lesion with florid ductal hyperplasia  usual type   see note   note  sections of the core biopsy demonstrate a few dilated ducts distended with benign proliferative ductal epithelial cells in the pattern of usual type florid ductal hyperplasia  the stroma surrounding these ducts is densely cellular with an increased number of spindle cells  in some areas  the stroma has a cloverleaf growth pattern  however  clear cut stromal overgrowth is not present  no atypical stromal cells or mitotic figures are noted  the slides for the prior phyllodes tumor  removed_accession_id  were reviewed and compared to the current sample  morphologically the two lesions are similar  particularly with regard to the level of stromal cellularity  overall  the findings are those of a low grade fibro epithelial lesion and favor a fibroadenoma  however  the differential diagnosis includes a low grade phyllodes 